<div class="thumb tright"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:276px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Conversation%20convert%20to%20cutscene.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/a/a2/Conversation_convert_to_cutscene.png" width="274" height="505" class="thumbimage" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Conversation%20convert%20to%20cutscene.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>The edit menu</div></div></div>
<p>When you run the "Process camera for line" or "Process camera for children" command in the conversation editor, either from the toolbar (the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Icon%20process%20cameras.png"><img alt="Icon process cameras.png" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/8/89/Icon_process_cameras.png" width="16" height="16" /></a> button) or the edit menu, the toolset will attempt to automatically assign cameras to make the conversation more active.
</p><p>Cameras will be chosen from the conversation's <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Stage" title="Stage">stage</a>. Specifically, from the <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Stage#Place_properties" title="Stage">place properties</a>. Make sure you set the "close", "default" and "wide" cameras for each place to an appropriate camera.
</p>
